{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 57,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to heart: and merciful men ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " taken away, none considering that the righteous is taken away from the evil ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to come",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "each one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " walking ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his uprightness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But draw near hither, ye sons of the sorceress, the seed of the adulterer and the lewd.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Against whom do ye sport yourselves? against whom make ye a wide mouth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thrust out the tongue? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye not children of transgression, a seed of falsehood,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Inflaming yourselves with idols under every green tree, slaying the children in the valleys under the cliffs of the rocks?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Among the smooth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "stones",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the stream ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy portion; they, they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy lot: even to them hast thou poured a drink-offering, thou hast offered a meat-offering. Should I receive comfort in these?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Upon a lofty and high mountain hast thou set thy bed: even thither thou wentest up to offer sacrifice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behind the doors also and the posts hast thou set up thy remembrance: for thou hast uncovered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thyself to another",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " than me, and hast gone up; thou hast enlarged thy bed, and made thee ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "a covenant",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with them; thou lovedst their bed where thou sawest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou wentest to the king with ointment, and didst increase thy perfumes, and didst send thy messengers far off, and didst debase ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thyself even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to hell.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art wearied in the greatness of thy way; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " saidst thou not, There is no hope: thou hast found the life of thy hand; therefore thou wast not grieved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And of whom hast thou been afraid or feared, that thou hast lied, and hast not remembered me, nor laid ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to thy heart? have not I held my peace even of old, and thou fearest me not?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will declare thy righteousness, and thy works; for they shall not profit thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou criest, let thy companies deliver thee; but the wind shall carry them all away; vanity shall take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": but he that putteth his trust in me shall possess the land, and shall inherit my holy mountain;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And shall say, Cast ye up, cast ye up, prepare the way, take up the stumbling-block out of the way of my people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thus saith the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Holy; I dwell in the high and holy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", with him also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of a contrite and humble spirit, to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite ones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I will not contend for ever, neither will I be always wroth: for the spirit would fail before me, and the souls ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I have made.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the iniquity of his covetousness I was wroth, and smote him: I hid me, and was wroth, and he went on frowardly in the way of his heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have seen his ways, and will heal him: I will lead him also, and restore comforts to him and to his mourners.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I create the fruit of the lips; Peace, peace to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " far off, and to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " near, saith the LORD; and I will heal him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like the troubled sea, when it cannot rest, whose waters cast up mire and dirt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.57.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.57.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no peace, saith my God, to the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
